        min-height: 100px;
        display: flex;
        align-items: center;
        justify-content: center;
        /* color: red;  If you use the class, you can remove this from here */
    }

    /* ... existing styles ... */
    ```

**Why Method 1 is better here:**

For this specific request, targeting the `id` (`#jokeDisplay`) is more direct and cleaner because you only have one element that needs to be red. Using a class is more about applying the same style to multiple elements.

